==="?/'From , cf. Lithuanian ''kiek'', with the meaning of ''how many''.===
From {{etyl|bat|fi}}, cf. Lithuanian ''kiek'', with the meaning of ''how many''.

===Pronoun===
'''kaikki''' (''singular/plural'')
# {{label|fi|indefinite|in singular, without a main word}} [[everything|Everything]].
#: ''[[tänään|Tänään]] '''kaikki''' [[mennä|menee]] [[pieleen]].''
#:: ''Today '''everything''' goes wrong.''
#: ''[[vihata|Vihaan]] '''kaikkea.'''
#:: ''I hate everything.''
# {{label|fi|indefinite|in plural, without a main word}} [[everyone|Everyone]], [[everybody]].
#: '''''Kaikki''' [[olla|olivat]] [[täällä]].''
#:: '''''Everyone''' was here.''
#: ''[[vihata|Vihaan]] '''kaikkia.'''
#:: ''I hate everyone.''
# {{label|fi|indefinite|in singular and plural, as a modifier}} [[all|All]].
#: '''''Kaikki''' [[sukka]][[-ni|ni]] [[löytyä|löytyivät]].''
#:: '''''All''' my socks were found.''
#: ''[[yhtäkkiä|Yhtäkkiä]] '''kaikki''' [[vesi]] [[vyöryä|vyöryi]] [[huoneisto]]on.''
#:: ''Suddenly '''all''' the water ran into the apartment.''
# As a former part of compound (in nominative or genitive) signifies [[all-]], [[omni-]].

====Declension====
====Usage notes====
* The pronoun has also a nominative plural form ''kaiket'' which is used only in some phrases, e.g. ''kaiket [[päivä]]t'', "day after day" / "for days on end".

====Synonyms====
* (''everyone'') [[jokainen]]

====Antonyms====
* (''all'', ''everything'') [[mikään|negation verb + mikään]]
* (''everyone'') [[kukaan|negation verb + kukaan]]

